    description: "FOUND 2026-10-24 alongside the kind-slot limb (INV-kurup, stage 10). id-format:F3's 'Symbol.id name-slot is empty' advisory, from four producers (grpc survey, dev 2aeec80eb3 code):\n  - starlark.py: depends_on edges use dst=f\"starlark:{rel_path}:{dep}\", the RAW label (\":name\", \"//pkg:name\", \"@repo//pkg:name\"), not a canonical id. Boundary synthesis then mints starlark:<unknown>:0-0::external_symbol, and 479 depends_on edges on grpc collapse onto that one nameless node.\n  - py.py: a base class that is a call expression (class X(collections.namedtuple(...)), and similar) gives an extends edge to python:external:0-0::external_symbol (30 on grpc).\n  - ruby.py: 1 calls edge to ruby:external:0-0::external_symbol (src/ruby/qps/proxy-worker.rb:161).\n  - cpp.py: an anonymous enum gets a symbol with an empty name (http2_settings.h:36-49::enum).\nFIX: per producer. Starlark: resolve \":name\" to the package's own target id and give other labels a canonical external dst (make_manifest_target_dst / make_unresolved_edge). Python and Ruby: emit no edge, or a named one, when the base or callee has no name. C++: name the anonymous enum per the language's convention for anonymous types, or emit none. Acceptance: 0 empty-name-slot advisories on the jahuf corpus surveys; no verdict change."  # 9bb3
    fields: {}  # 9bb3
